## Context

- Phase 2 baselines: BOTH FAILED
  - PD severity (UCI PD Telemonitoring): LOSO-CV AUROC=0.369. Dataset has no healthy controls (all 42 subjects have PD). Between-subject voice variability dominates severity signal.
  - Respiratory (COUGHVID): 5-fold CV AUROC=0.524. Self-reported crowd-sourced labels too noisy for handcrafted features.
  - MCI: deferred (ADReSS/DementiaBank requires restricted access)
- Feature importance analysis (task #1503): BLOCKED — meaningless without working classifiers
- Created task #1589 for data_curator: download UCI Parkinson's Dataset with healthy controls
- Created task #1600 for research_director: review baseline failures, decide path forward
- Phase 2 summary written to output/diagnostics/acoustic-multi-disease-panel/phase2_baselines.md
- Project cannot advance to Phase 3 (multi-disease panel) until 2+ conditions achieve AUROC >= 0.75
- Key recommendations: (1) better datasets with clinical labels, (2) try deep learning on spectrograms, (3) may need to pivot project scope
